A||||4||Leadfoot||Electronic decklid lock not working||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||10:28 AM||||I just replaced the clutch pedal with the one from the fiero store.  Right after the transplant my electronic decklid lock stopped working.  Is it possible that I bumped something while I was working under the dash?||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT-maniac||07-02-2001||03:45 PM||||I'd check fuses first, you may have knocked one loose down there. Then I would check the neutral start switch. If it's not working there won't be any power to the decklid switch because it's designed to work only when the ignition is off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||07-02-2001||04:33 PM||||Actually, the trunk switch will work while the car is running.......an auto must be in park and a manual must have the e-brake on.<P>As for your problem......it is probably just a coincidence that it failed after replacing the clutch pedal, so I would inspect the switch itself. Take the bezel off of the speedo pod (four T-15 torx screws) and unplug the switch.  Now shake the whole thing......if you hear a rattle the switch has broken.<P>     ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-02-2001||05:31 PM||||To clarify, I have a manual and the car was off when I tried the switch.  I do hear a clicking noise which seems to be coming from under the dash.  Would that noise be coming from a relay?||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||07-02-2001||05:54 PM||||The relay is under the dash on right side. the the solenoid gets it ground thru the latch when the trunk lid is shut.(I don't like this set up). Therefore the latch will not work with trunk up. It has to be shut. open the trunk and attach a ground wire to the latch and frame or engine and see if it works. mine does not work half the time and I found this to be the problem. someday I am going to run a separate wire for the ground. <BR>hope this helps.||||reg||1
